  "reasoning": "The patient reports leg swelling significant enough to make shoes tight, along with discomfort that worsens after prolonged sitting. These symptoms are classic signs of venous insufficiency, where impaired blood return leads to fluid accumulation (edema) and venous pooling. Prolonged sitting exacerbates this by further hindering venous return. Among the listed possibilities, varicose veins is the condition most directly associated with isolated lower extremity swelling and positional discomfort without other systemic symptoms.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]varicose veins[/DIAGNOSIS]"
